# Prefer existing core algorithms

View / demo / interaction code may only **call** core methods. Do not reimplement layout, height, connect, add, delete, paste, or rename.

## Must use (do not replace)

| Task | Use this |
|------|----------|
| Add / drop | `transformData.add` + `addCheck` |
| Connect open branch / FB pin | `ifCanConnectOB` + `connectOB` |
| Move / paste | `moveElements` / `paste` |
| Delete element or line | `deleteArr` / `deleteLine` |
| Rename title or FB pin | `calculateVarHeight` / `calculateFBVarHeight` then `setVarName` |
| Layout after mutation | `updateCanvas` (or demo `refreshLadLayout` — same order) |
| Pin align / FBL height | existing `initHeight.FBL` (`offsetPin0` / `pinOffsetFirstPin`) |
| Lines | `calculateLines` → `lineMap` |

## Do not

- Invent a second height, connect, or layout formula in the view layer
- Mutate `linkedList` fields that those methods already write (`varName`, `varNameHeight`, `connectId`, pin offsets)
- Change `calculate.ts` formulas unless fixing a proven layout bug
- Add new data-model fields when an existing one already stores the value

## Demo vs production

- Production: `ladEvent` → `index.*` wrappers (`setVarName`, `add`, …)
- Demo (`invokeCoreOnDrop`): call the **same** core functions (`transformData.*`, height helpers), then `updateCanvas` / `refreshLadLayout`
- Demo must not skip the height / check / connect helpers just because it cannot construct a full `Lad`
